From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: rockchip: rock-pi-4c: cap SPI NOR frequency at 1 MHz

The upstream device tree sets spi-max-frequency = <108000000> for the
XT25F32B SPI NOR. At this rate the JEDEC ID reads back as ff ff ff.
At 24 MHz the chip probes and reads, but writes fail: sf write leaves
the flash erased. At 1 MHz erase, write and read-back pass every time.
Cap the rate in the U-Boot overlay.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 arch/arm/dts/rk3399-rock-pi-4c-u-boot.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-rock-pi-4c-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-rock-pi-4c-u-boot.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-rock-pi-4c-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-rock-pi-4c-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 &spi1 {
 	flash@0 {
+		spi-max-frequency = <1000000>;
 		bootph-pre-ram;
 		bootph-some-ram;
 	};
